# THE SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH FOR "WHAT IS NOT ON THE SITE".
#
# rsync reads this with --exclude-from to build the deploy artifact, and
# tools/deploy_should_run.mjs reads the SAME file to decide whether a push
# changed anything the site actually serves. Keeping two hand-maintained copies
# of this list is how a push gets skipped that should have deployed — the exact
# two-sources-of-truth defect that shipped a phone game picker listing one disc
# of five. One file, both readers.
#
# rsync semantics, unchanged from the inline list this replaces: a pattern with
# a leading slash is anchored at the deploy root, one without matches ANY path
# component at any depth.
.git
.github
.claude
_deploy
# The list itself is not a served file. It used to be excluded by a separate
# `--exclude='/deploy.exclude'` flag in the workflow, which made it the ONE
# exclusion not expressed here — enough to make tools/verify_artifact_complete.mjs
# report a false MISSING, since that check derives "what belongs in the artifact"
# from this file alone. One list, no exceptions.
/deploy.exclude
emsdk
node_modules
*.tsbuildinfo
ps1/ps1Wasm/pcsx-wasm-src
ps1/ps1Wasm/wasmpsx-repo
/bementalJIT
/gamecube/bementalJIT
gamecube/dolphin-src
gamecube/build-*
gamecube/ppc-worker/build-*
gamecube/tools
dolphin_captures/*.log
dolphin_captures/*.txt
research_findings.md
/tools
/build-*
*.iso
*.bin.bak
*.o
*.a
Makefile*
handler.js
serverless.yml
send.email.js
send.email.ts
/dreamcast/states/pso2_pioneer2_*
/ps1/duckstation-master
/gamecube/docs
/dreamcast/docs

# ─── OFFSITE-BEGIN ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT "not on the site" — SERVED FROM A DIFFERENT REPO, SAME ORIGIN.
#
# The game library lives in Bemental77/gamedata, whose GitHub Pages site is
# published at https://caseybement.com/gamedata/ — a *project* Pages site under
# the same custom apex domain as this one. Same origin means no CORS and no
# cross-origin-isolation problem, which is load-bearing: these pages need
# SharedArrayBuffer and run under COOP/COEP via coi-serviceworker.js, whose
# scope is `/` and which rewrites no URLs (it re-stamps COEP/CORP/COOP onto
# whatever it proxies). A real CDN on another host would have needed CORP
# headers on every ROM; this needs none.
#
# WHY. Measured on run 34290489234, the last deploy that actually published:
#   checkout 345 s · stage 48 s · upload 341 s · deploy 223 s = 960 s
# 909 of those 960 s were moving the library, on EVERY push, including one-line
# HTML edits. Deploys were slower than the interval between pushes, so each new
# push cancelled the pending one and fixes never reached production at all —
# four Dreamcast games sat broken live with their fix committed and pushed.
# MEASURED FOR THE FOUR PATHS BELOW, staged the way the workflow stages it
# (rsync --exclude-from into a scratch dir, then `du -sh` and
# `find -type f | wc -l`) from a TRACKED-ONLY mirror, because a tracked-only
# tree is what the CI checkout materialises — rsyncing the whole working tree
# instead measures 12 GiB / 22,832 files and is not the artifact:
#   before   9.1 GiB · 2056 files   (this file with no OFFSITE block)
#   after    2.8 GiB · 1921 files   (the four paths below)
# Of the 2.8 GiB that remains, 2.5 GiB is /dreamcast/discs — see DEFERRED below.
#
# The files remain tracked in this repo (local dev, tools/audit_all.mjs and the
# probe rigs all read them from the working tree) — they are only kept out of
# the deploy artifact, and out of the CI checkout via the sparse-checkout that
# .github/workflows/deploy.yml DERIVES FROM THIS BLOCK. That derivation is why
# the markers exist; do not rename them without updating the workflow.
#
# ⚠ EDITING THESE FILES IN *THIS* REPO NO LONGER CHANGES THE SITE. They are
# still tracked here (local dev, tools/audit_all.mjs and the probe rigs all read
# them from the working tree) but the published bytes come from the gamedata
# repo. Add or replace a ROM/disc in BOTH places, or the catalogs will name a
# URL that does not resolve — and note the deploy job will correctly report
# `deploy=false` for such a push, because nothing in THIS artifact changed.
# `node tools/verify_live_catalogs.mjs` is what catches the mismatch.
#
# TO REVERT: delete this block, and set ASSET_BASE back to '' in lib/asset_base.js
# — ONE line, whole site. Proven in both directions: with '' all 207 catalog URLs
# resolve at the old paths, with '/gamedata' all 207 resolve at the new ones.
#
# ⚠ DEFERRED ON PURPOSE — /dreamcast/discs IS DELIBERATELY NOT LISTED BELOW.
# dreamcast.html's ASSET_BASE conversion exists but is still UNCOMMITTED, and
# the ORDER is the whole risk: excluding the discs while the DEPLOYED page still
# fetches '/dreamcast/discs/...' 404s all five Dreamcast games the instant it
# ships. Keeping them is safe in BOTH directions and costs only artifact size —
# the deployed page finds them here, and the converted page finds them on
# gamedata (verified with a ranged GET: /gamedata/dreamcast/discs/pso2/Track1.bin
# answers 206). Add the line in the SAME commit that lands the converted
# dreamcast.html, never before. Measured, that step takes the artifact from
# 2.8 GiB / 1921 files to 237 MiB / 1845 files.
/gamecube/roms
/ps1/ps1Wasm/roms
/n64/N64Wasm/roms
/gba/gbaWasm/roms
# ─── OFFSITE-END ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
